DESCRIPTION:Event Details:Create spirited crafts such as painted acorns\,
  rangoli sand art\, lantern making\, fabric ghost hangs\, and leaf rubbin
 gs.Crafts not your jam? Relax with your choice of flavored popcorn from P
 opKornTwist and a cup of apple cider while watching a captivating Dia de 
 los Muertos performance by Ballet Folklórico. Or\, get your face painted
  and snap a selfie at our polaroid station to capture a memory to save fo
 r years.This program is free and open to all\, with Museum galleries rema
 ining open for the entirety of the event to give a special\, after-hours 
 view of the exhibitions.&#160\;Parking Information:Limitedcomplimentary p
 arkingis available in front of theMuseum entranceoff Indiana Avenue. Stre
 et parking is free on weekdays after 5:00 PM in the neighborhoods surroun
 ding the Museum. Paid parking options include theUniversity Collections a
 t McCallaparking lot off Indiana Avenue\, theIndiana Memorial Unionvisito
 r lot\, and nearby metered street parking. Convenient metered street park
 ing is available in the downtown/Sample Gates area along Kirkwood Avenue\
 , East 6th Street\, East 4th Street\, North Lincoln Street\, North Dunn S
 treet\, and South Grant Street.Questions?  For accessibility assistance o
